# Multi-command / compound handling (do not lose a step, do not split a single intent)

A "compound" prompt asks for **two or more actions** in one message. Target: every reasonable multi-action request decomposes into ordered steps with **shared context**, and single-action prompts are **never** falsely split.

## Detect → decompose (deterministic-first)

All in `backend/src/modules/ai/intent-decomposition.util.ts`:

- `COMPOUND_PROMPT_MARKERS` — connectors ("and then", ";", "also", "after that", "плюс", "հետո", …).
- `isCompoundPrompt(prompt)` — gate; if false, route as a single intent.
- `GOLDEN_COMPOUND_PATTERNS` + `matchGoldenCompoundPattern()` — high-confidence known shapes (e.g. check-and-book, cancel-and-notify). Golden match wins over generic split.
- `decomposeDeterministicForSurface(surface, prompt)` — produces ordered `DecomposedIntentStep[]`.
- `decomposeCustomerSelfServiceCompound()` — customer-surface helper.
- `validateStepsAgainstRecipe()` / `getCompoundRecipeById()` — enforce a recipe's allowed steps.

Decomposition source is typed: `DecompositionSource = 'deterministic' | 'golden' | 'llm'` (`intent-decomposition.types.ts`). Only fall back to `llm` decomposition when deterministic + golden both miss.

## Recipes & routing

- Compound recipes: `COMPOUND_COMMAND_RECIPES` in `ai-command-registry.ts` (`examplePrompts`, `surfaces`, `decomposeUtil`, `llmDecompose`).
- The complexity router tags compound prompts with `routeTier: 'compound'` (`command-complexity-router.service.ts`). Compound tier unlocks the multi-step executor.
- **Today decomposition is deterministic/golden.** LangGraph compound graphs (`booking-command-graph` / `compound-command-graph`) are **planned (`ai-cmd-h2.4`)** behind `LANGGRAPH_ENABLED` — do not assume those files exist; extend the deterministic util unless you are implementing that task.

## Shared context across steps (the #1 correctness bug)

Every sub-step must inherit entities resolved earlier: `date`, `timeOfDay`, `notBeforeTime`, `serviceName`, provider, `allProviders`. Reference helpers (verified): `enrichBookingTimeHintsFromPrompt`, `bookingFirstAvailable`, and the check→book compound (`check_and_book_compound`) in `ai-payments.util.ts` + `customer-ai-command.util.ts`.

Rules:
- Resolve shared booking context **once** from the prompt, then merge into each step — never re-classify each clause in isolation.
- A "check who's free + book the soonest" prompt forwards the availability result into the book step (no second lookup, no dropped time hint).
- Action names differ per surface — a dashboard compound uses `check_providers_for_service` → `book_nearest_slot`; public uses `check_availability` → `book_appointment`. Decompose to the **right verbs for that surface**.

## Reference implementation (copy this shape)

`ai-cmd-h1` check+book: `ai-check-and-book.fixtures.ts` (scenarios + per-surface rules), decomposition in `ai-payments.util.ts`, `ai-check-and-book.integration.spec.ts`.

## Eval coverage (mandatory for any compound work)

Add cases to `eval/ai-command-eval.cases.ts` (mapped from `intent-decomposition.fixtures.ts` `COMPOUND_DECOMPOSITION_SCENARIOS` via `compoundScenarioToEvalCase`). Use these expectation fields (`ai-command-eval.types.ts`):

- `routeTier: 'compound'`, `compoundSurface`
- `compoundSteps` (exact ordered actions) **or** `compoundActionsContains` (subset, any order) **or** `compoundMinSteps`
- `compoundStepParams` (per-step param subset — proves shared context propagated)
- `compoundSource` / `compoundRecipeId` when stable
- `compoundExpectEmpty: true` for single-intent prompts that must **not** split (false-compound guard)

## Definition of done (compound)

- [ ] `isCompoundPrompt` true only for genuine multi-action prompts; add a `compoundExpectEmpty` eval guard for the nearest single-intent phrasing.
- [ ] Golden pattern added when the shape recurs; otherwise deterministic split per surface.
- [ ] Shared context (date/time/service/provider) asserted to flow into every step via `compoundStepParams`.
- [ ] Per-surface decomposition + verbs (dashboard, provider, customer, public where applicable).
- [ ] Integration spec mirrors `ai-check-and-book.integration.spec.ts` (2-step and 3+-step flows).
- [ ] `npm run test:sprint14` (eval) + the relevant `test:ai-*` suite pass.

